# tag -> (options, preset, b tolerance, se tolerance); tolerances are relative (max over parameters).
#   Iterative ML / quadrature fits stop at Stata's ml convergence criteria (nrtolerance 1e-5): 1e-6 for b, 1e-5 for SE.
#   GEE: Stata xtgee stops when the relative coefficient change is <= 1e-6 (e(dif) ~ 1e-7): 1e-6.
#   Robust VCE of the quadrature models: Stata recomputes the scores with me<cmd> ..., iter(0) (gsem's own adaptive
#   quadrature at the posted estimates, [XT] _xt_robust.ado), so the sandwich differs from ours by the node placement
